OL,4,CNext data accessed in cyber breach     
OL,5,GNext has said that some of its data    
OL,6,Ghas been accessed in a cyber breach    
OL,7,Gaffecting a third-party online         
OL,8,Gsupplier.                              
OL,10,FThe high street retailer said there    
OL,11,Fwas no evidence that customers'        
OL,12,Fpersonal data had been compromised.    
OL,14,FThe firm - which has its headquarters  
OL,15,Fin Enderby, Leicestershire - said it   
OL,16,Fhad been informed by one of its        
OL,17,Fsuppliers about the incident, which    
OL,18,Fled to "unauthorised access to certain 
OL,19,Fbenign data relating to Next".         
